# f1 = fill, f2 = again, f3 = seen. The typed copy of a loop held its store against the length that the list had in front of the loop, so a loop that fills a list from its own end left the copy at its first store, for good.
# In fill() the list is a literal born for this entry into the loop, and the counter enters with the number of values written. That the list is still as long is asked once, in front. Every turn stores once under the counter,
# which goes up by one, and no turn writes the storage: at every head the list is as long as the counter is great. The count alone ends this loop, so whether the room holds every turn is asked once, in front, and the turn only raises the length.
# In again() nobody knows how long the list is: it is stored into as before, and its length stays read once in front.
# In seen() the array grows in the iterations, once, to the bound: each store at the end asks the length, and holds it against the capacity that is read before the loop, with the storage, and again where the array has grown.
# RUN(FILL): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# FILL: [[room]]: {{*}} = GetArrayCapacity
# FILL: LessEq {{*}}, [[room]]
# FILL: isLoopHead=true
# FILL-NOT: GetArrayLength
# FILL-NOT: Less {{*}}, [[room]]
# FILL: ExtendArrayLength
# FILL-NEXT: Put{{*}}Index
# RUN(AGAIN): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# AGAIN-NOT: ExtendArrayLength
# RUN(SEEN): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# SEEN: ReserveArrayCapacity
# SEEN: isLoopHead=true
# SEEN: isLoopHead=true
# SEEN: [[storage]]: opaque(ArrayStoragePointer) @RawWord = GetArrayStorage
# SEEN: [[room]]: {{*}} = GetArrayCapacity
# SEEN: [[length]]: {{*}} = GetArrayLength
# SEEN: StrictEq {{*}}, [[length]] form=Integers
# SEEN: Less {{*}}, [[room]]
# SEEN: ExtendArrayLength {{*}}, [[storage]]
# SEEN: PutContiguousIndex {{*}} storage=[[storage]]
# SEEN: ReserveArrayCapacity
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
